# Upload as `.htaccess` at the FTP home — the folder that contains www/, voyage/
# and voyage-private/, NOT inside voyage/.
#
# Why: a hostname pointed at this hosting without a Multisite entry of its own
# gets the FTP home as its document root. www.voyage.kemen.fr did exactly that and
# served a browsable index of every site on the account. The .env was still refused
# (403) and PHP still executed rather than being handed over as source, so nothing
# secret leaked — but the layout of the whole account was on display.
#
# This is defence in depth. The actual fix is to give the hostname a document root
# in the OVH Multisite panel; keep this anyway, so the next hostname that appears
# without one fails closed.

# No directory listings, anywhere below this point.
Options -Indexes

# Dotfiles and the things that should never be fetched over HTTP, whichever
# document root a request arrives through.
<FilesMatch "(^\.|\.(env|sql|log|ini|sh|lock|bak|dist)$)">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
